    "id": "x-ip-offline",
    "type": "single",
    "topic": "instr-instrumentation",
    "stem": "In an offline processing pipeline, what do the docs suggest to see how long items take to pass through?",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "A timestamped heartbeat through each stage",
        "correct": true,
        "note": "This is the correct answer."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "A summary per item with an item_id label",
        "correct": false,
        "note": "Per-item labels explode cardinality."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Polling the database row count per stage",
        "correct": false,
        "note": "Doesn't show per-stage latency."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Graphing irate() of the queue size",
        "correct": false,
        "note": "That's not how the docs suggest it."
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "For offline processing, send a heartbeat through the system that includes the timestamp; each stage exports the most recent heartbeat timestamp it saw.",
